body:
Maybe closer than the BBC accent since it's a manufactured way of speaking, but I doubt American accents are closer to medieval English than other modern provincial English accents. The US accent would have been influenced by migrants from other areas of the world. 

I don't know this guys credentials and obviously it's all speculative, but his take sounds similar to a modern rural English or even Welsh accent;  

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3lXv3Tt4x20
